/// known-gap: interp reads a bare name in a method as the object's field when it has one
/// Inside a class method, a name that is not a local reads the program's
/// variable of that name. The object's field is `@name` (`self >> name`),
/// never the bare name.
lim | 3
a | 99
<>P |
    a: 1
    act check()
        if @a < lim
            say("less")
        xx
        y | lim + 1
        say("y {y}, a {a}, @a {@a}")
    xx
xx
p <> P | a: 1
p.check()
